WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.573
The next morning, the Earthworms rode their bikes to the end of Old Church Road.

2
00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.395
Katie was confused.

3
00:00:09.396 --> 00:00:13.284
"Do we go this way or that way?" she asked.

4
00:00:13.285 --> 00:00:15.897
"We need a GPS!"

5
00:00:15.898 --> 00:00:18.165
But Luke knew the way.

6
00:00:18.166 --> 00:00:22.353
He led them over an old bridge and down a dirt road.

7
00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:24.848
"We're getting close!"

8
00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:29.427
A few moments later, they stopped in front of an old house.

9
00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:31.450
"This is it," he said.

10
00:00:31.451 --> 00:00:33.698
It looked deserted.

11
00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:37.041
"Creepy," said Katie.

12
00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:40.815
" Nobody lives here," said

13
00:00:40.816 --> 00:00:44.629
Emily. "Let's go home," said

14
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.897
AJ. "Shh. Listen," said

15
00:00:47.898 --> 00:00:54.300
Emily. Someone was

16
00:00:54.301 --> 00:00:57.719
singing. They left their bikes and followed the

17
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:03.483
voice. An old woman was hanging clothes to dry, singing as she

18
00:01:03.484 --> 00:01:09.875
worked. She fastened the last piece to the line, picked up her basket, and turned

19
00:01:09.876 --> 00:01:13.276
around. "Who are you?" she

20
00:01:13.277 --> 00:01:16.809
snapped. "She seems crabby," thought

21
00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:20.000
Katie. "We're the Earthworms!" said

22
00:01:20.001 --> 00:01:22.496
AJ. Emily pushed her

23
00:01:22.497 --> 00:01:25.338
brother. "I'm Emily," she

24
00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:29.322
said. "Luke." "AJ."

25
00:01:29.323 --> 00:01:31.527
"Katie." "What are you doing

26
00:01:31.528 --> 00:01:36.142
here? I never have visitors," the old woman

27
00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:40.612
said. "We're on a scavenger hunt," Katie

28
00:01:40.613 --> 00:01:42.647
replied. The woman looked

29
00:01:42.648 --> 00:01:46.057
doubtful. "What are you hunting out

30
00:01:46.058 --> 00:01:49.117
here?" "You!" said

31
00:01:49.118 --> 00:01:53.655
AJ. "The oldest person in Willow Creek," said

32
00:01:53.656 --> 00:01:58.176
Emily. "You're Ms. Cora Mae Henderson, right?" said

33
00:01:58.177 --> 00:02:02.165
Katie. "Your brother drew us a map so we could find

34
00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:07.318
you." "My brother is a busybody," said Ms.

35
00:02:07.319 --> 00:02:11.163
Henderson. "He has a Model T!" said

36
00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.782
AJ. Ms. Henderson finally

37
00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:18.387
smiled. "Oh, yes. I've heard all about

38
00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:22.637
it. Brother says he will take me for a ride

39
00:02:22.638 --> 00:02:25.657
soon." Ms. Henderson looked up at the back

40
00:02:25.658 --> 00:02:30.364
porch. "If you don't mind, I'd like to sit

41
00:02:30.365 --> 00:02:33.818
down." When everyone was comfortable, Luke

42
00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:38.868
said, "Your brother says his Model T was the first car in Willow

43
00:02:38.869 --> 00:02:42.436
Creek." "That could be true," she

44
00:02:42.437 --> 00:02:48.379
said. "I was a school girl when Randolph Patterson bought that Model

45
00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.248
T. Folks didn't like it

46
00:02:51.249 --> 00:02:57.178
though. When that car raced down the road, dust clouds filled the air.

47
00:02:57.179 --> 00:02:58.940
You couldn't breathe.

48
00:02:58.941 --> 00:03:03.692
The farmers, like my daddy, said the dust hurt the crops.

49
00:03:03.693 --> 00:03:09.598
And if it was washing day, the ladies had to take everything off the line.

50
00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:13.779
They had to wash their laundry all over again."

51
00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:20.060
"Your brother is going to drive his Model T in the Willow Creek birthday parade," said Luke.

52
00:03:20.061 --> 00:03:25.475
"Willow Creek is turning 150 years old," said Katie.

53
00:03:25.476 --> 00:03:30.037
"My, my. Time passes quickly.

54
00:03:30.038 --> 00:03:35.507
When Willow Creek turned fifty, I was just a little girl.

55
00:03:35.508 --> 00:03:43.057
When it turned one hundred, I had gray hair!" Ms. Henderson laughed.

56
00:03:43.058 --> 00:03:48.633
"And now the town is 150 already?"

57
00:03:48.634 --> 00:03:53.474
"Yep. And we're going to be in the parade," said Emily.

58
00:03:53.475 --> 00:03:57.222
"You could be in it too!" said Katie.

59
00:03:57.223 --> 00:04:01.403
"Oh, no, I don't go to town anymore,"

60
00:04:01.404 --> 00:04:04.515
said Ms. Henderson, shaking her head.

61
00:04:04.516 --> 00:04:07.745
"It's too busy now."

62
00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:12.223
"You could ride in the Model T!" said AJ.

63
00:04:12.224 --> 00:04:15.205
"We're going," said Emily.

64
00:04:15.206 --> 00:04:21.054
"Well, I have to think about it," said Ms. Henderson.

65
00:04:21.055 --> 00:04:27.271
"Ms. Henderson, will you write a note for our scavenger bag?" asked Katie.

66
00:04:27.272 --> 00:04:33.567
Ms. Henderson smiled. "I did many scavenger hunts when I was a girl."

67
00:04:33.568 --> 00:04:36.326
She happily wrote out a note.

68
00:04:36.327 --> 00:04:40.370
It said: My name is Cora Mae Henderson.

69
00:04:40.371 --> 00:04:43.824
I am 103 years old.

70
00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:46.969
The Earthworms got on their bikes.

71
00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.471
"Hope to see you at the parade!"

72
00:04:49.472 --> 00:04:53.414
they called and headed back down the road.

73
00:04:53.415 --> 00:04:59.497
The next morning, Mrs. Penkov led the campers on a hike along Willow Creek.

74
00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:01.623
She showed them turtle eggs.

75
00:05:01.624 --> 00:05:05.441
She showed them a lizard sleeping in the sun.

76
00:05:05.442 --> 00:05:08.663
The campers picked wildflowers.

77
00:05:08.664 --> 00:05:11.954
Katie was thinking about Ms. Henderson.

78
00:05:11.955 --> 00:05:16.693
Did she walk along the creek when she was eight years old?

79
00:05:16.694 --> 00:05:19.814
What did the creek look like back then?

80
00:05:19.815 --> 00:05:22.798
Suddenly Emily grabbed Katie's arm.

81
00:05:22.799 --> 00:05:25.862
"Did you hear?" she whispered.

82
00:05:25.863 --> 00:05:31.661
"The Tornadoes are going to the senior home today to look for the oldest person."

83
00:05:31.662 --> 00:05:38.972
"HA!" said Katie. "They'll never find her there!"

